WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:07.073
Patrick, this walkthrough shows the current vehicle first workflow and the latest barcode integrity changes.

2
00:00:07.023 --> 00:00:11.108
We will also check the console updates and record controls.

3
00:00:11.947 --> 00:00:14.642
Step one is the vehicle barcode.

4
00:00:14.592 --> 00:00:19.025
The field opens in scan mode, with keyboard input suppressed.

5
00:00:19.025 --> 00:00:23.367
Tapping the field enables typing and marks the entry as manual.

6
00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:26.396
There is no separate manual entry button.

7
00:00:27.238 --> 00:00:30.397
Step two is the driver employee number.

8
00:00:30.347 --> 00:00:33.285
This field also opens scan ready.

9
00:00:33.285 --> 00:00:37.989
After the driver, choose the direction, then review and submit.

10
00:00:38.822 --> 00:00:41.890
Employee numbers can contain letters.

11
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.441
Here, A B one two three identifies our demonstration driver.

12
00:00:46.441 --> 00:00:56.905
Numeric forms one zero zero three, E one zero zero three, and E M P dash one zero zero three all resolve to E one zero zero three.

13
00:00:57.738 --> 00:01:02.456
With the vehicle and driver captured, choose Vehicle In or Vehicle Out.

14
00:01:02.406 --> 00:01:05.229
The next screen is the review step.

15
00:01:06.072 --> 00:01:10.287
Choose the direction, then review the movement before submitting.

16
00:01:10.237 --> 00:01:13.781
The scanner returns to the start after recording it.

17
00:01:14.613 --> 00:01:18.520
This unknown barcode arrived through the scanner input path.

18
00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:21.833
It advances without the typed barcode warning.

19
00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:26.872
When submitted, its vehicle record is created without a Check barcode flag.

20
00:01:26.872 --> 00:01:29.655
Normal driver checks still apply.

21
00:01:30.488 --> 00:01:33.982
When typing is needed, tap the barcode field.

22
00:01:33.932 --> 00:01:37.824
That tap enables typing and records manual entry.

23
00:01:37.824 --> 00:01:41.935
A partial barcode such as G zero zero is refused.

24
00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:44.254
Enter all four digits.

25
00:01:45.072 --> 00:01:50.292
A complete typed barcode that is not in inventory warns: Check this barcode.

26
00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:52.562
Continue if it is right.

27
00:01:52.562 --> 00:01:58.193
The movement can proceed, and the vehicle is marked Check barcode for supervisor review.

28
00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:02.898
Here is the vehicle created from the typed unknown barcode.

29
00:02:02.848 --> 00:02:05.824
Check barcode is visible on its record.

30
00:02:05.824 --> 00:02:09.974
The unknown scanned vehicle was verified without that flag.

31
00:02:09.974 --> 00:02:12.577
That distinction is deliberate.

32
00:02:13.405 --> 00:02:17.865
The scanned vehicle can leave through the normal driver and license checks.

33
00:02:17.815 --> 00:02:21.630
This is the exit review screen, before submission.

34
00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:25.277
Missing inventory details do not block the movement.

35
00:02:26.113 --> 00:02:28.873
This is the actual role refusal.

36
00:02:28.823 --> 00:02:33.062
Casey Rowe holds the Scanner role and cannot approve the override.

37
00:02:33.062 --> 00:02:41.271
This driver has a current license but lacks authorization, so we are showing a role refusal, not an expired license screen.

38
00:02:42.113 --> 00:02:44.705
Authorization is selectable.

39
00:02:44.655 --> 00:02:50.970
The choices are nine hours, twelve hours, today, forty eight hours, and three days.

40
00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.707
Nine hours is the default, not a fixed duration.

41
00:02:55.530 --> 00:03:00.364
This is the desktop supervisor console, showing vehicle inventory.

42
00:03:00.314 --> 00:03:05.391
Records open through their identifiers instead of separate per row Edit buttons.

43
00:03:06.238 --> 00:03:11.137
A vehicle opens from its V I N, or Add V I N when missing.

44
00:03:11.087 --> 00:03:19.785
The removal control is available in the vehicle record, so supervisors can remove a vehicle from active inventory without deleting its history.

45
00:03:20.613 --> 00:03:26.414
Adding a vehicle requires only its V I N. Leave the optional barcode blank and save.

46
00:03:26.364 --> 00:03:30.049
The application assigns the next free G barcode.

47
00:03:30.863 --> 00:03:33.275
The vehicle has been saved.

48
00:03:33.225 --> 00:03:40.738
Here the next free barcode was G zero zero zero six, and the inventory shows it beside the V I N we entered.

49
00:03:41.572 --> 00:03:46.882
In the user list, select the User I D or name to open that existing user.

50
00:03:46.832 --> 00:03:50.402
The old per row Edit and Remove controls are gone.

51
00:03:51.238 --> 00:03:53.946
This is the existing user record.

52
00:03:53.896 --> 00:03:59.218
The available roles are Scanner, Fleet Lead, Supervisor, and Admin.

53
00:03:59.218 --> 00:04:03.664
These are prototype accounts, with the limitations shown in the form.

54
00:04:04.488 --> 00:04:07.557
Device records open from Device I D.

55
00:04:07.507 --> 00:04:11.695
The list retains operational status and history controls.

56
00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:18.150
The selected device opens here, with its location and configuration details.

57
00:04:18.947 --> 00:04:21.719
Movement history remains searchable.

58
00:04:21.669 --> 00:04:24.465
This is a device local review build.

59
00:04:24.465 --> 00:04:28.615
Shared cloud data and synchronization remain future work.

60
00:04:28.615 --> 00:04:33.061
The videos are ready for review, with deployment handled separately.
